00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:52,000
Oh, it's my lips. Oh,
shit. I can't breathe.

253
00:16:52,260 --> 00:16:53,100
Stop the car!

254
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:56,457
Giorno, turn the damn thing into
a freaking frog if you gotta.

255
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:57,737
I don't care what you do.

256
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:58,650
Just do it fast.

257
00:16:58,733 --> 00:17:00,737
Sorry, I already tried that before.

258
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:04,408
Problem is, nothing can survive
at minus 100 degrees Celsius.

259
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:13,480
Everyone knows the capital of France,
but English speakers pronounce it Paris,

260
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:16,662
while most say Paris the
way it's supposed to be.

261
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:21,460
But somehow Venice has replaced the
real Venice as the global standard.

262
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:25,526
Like those stories, The Merchant
of Venice and Death in Venice.

263
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:27,670
Why?

264
00:17:27,753 --> 00:17:29,680
Call the damn book Death in Venice!

265
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:31,040
It's not that hard!

266
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:32,613
Are we not good enough?

267
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:37,137
Learn a little Italian, puttana, and
call the thing what it's supposed to be!

268
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:39,985
What kind of puppet
bullshit are they on about?

269
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:47,715
So the cold is finally starting
to affect your driving.

270
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:52,360
Sorry about golden wind, Mista,
but I can't use it without warmth.

271
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:57,149
I'm really sorry about all this, but
there's not much I can do at this point.

272
00:17:57,420 --> 00:17:59,040
Besides picking up bullets.

273
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:04,357
It seems you've about reached your limit
as far as blowing holes in the car.

274
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:07,381
Now I'll put your body
into an even deeper freeze.

275
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,130
Huh?

276
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:17,117
Bullets retain a little heat
after being fired, right?

277
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:21,376
So, if I fire the ones Giorno picked
up, then I'm packing literal heat.

278
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:26,905
Speaking of him, he's at a loss for words,
so I'll do him a solid just this once.

279
00:18:27,260 --> 00:18:29,380
Get rid of this freak, golden wind!

280
00:18:37,120 --> 00:18:37,950
Success!

281
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:40,140
I know the sprouts don't look like much,

282
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:42,317
but those little plant
roots are strong enough to

283
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:45,337
tear up asphalt and demolish
boulders into pieces!

284
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:47,067
Hold on to the wheel, Torno!

285
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:48,240
We've gotta move!

286
00:18:57,460 --> 00:19:01,400
Just as Malone said, the newbie
must have pulled this stunt.

287
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,780
But you don't get off that easy!

288
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:09,700
Give me a break. Already?

289
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,240
He's after us again!

290
00:19:11,840 --> 00:19:16,722
I'll swoop in and make off with the goods
before those fools even know what's what.

291
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:20,260
You're wasting your bullets.

292
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:23,077
White Ice's specialty
is freezing the moisture

293
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,572
in the air at extremely low temperatures.

294
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:28,140
That's how I create my shimmering armor.

295
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:32,160
It's great for skating
on almost any surface.

296
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:36,120
And an added benefit is the way
it stops your pesky bullets!

297
00:19:36,660 --> 00:19:37,490
It's...

298
00:19:37,620 --> 00:19:38,450
Pastor Giorno!

299
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:39,973
It can't go any faster!

300
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:42,137
The tires are slipping all over the road!

301
00:19:42,220 --> 00:19:45,117
What's worse, these guys know all
about what's waiting at the station!

302
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,117
That may be true,

303
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:48,917
but they still don't have the clues
to where Trish and the turtle are,

304
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:52,057
which, if you ask me, is a
pretty damn good silver lining.

305
00:19:52,140 --> 00:19:53,977
There's that trademark optimism.

306
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:56,040
Yet again, you're a special one.

307
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:57,457
He's catching up!

308
00:19:57,540 --> 00:19:58,370
Step on it!

309
00:19:58,453 --> 00:19:59,637
Look, we can't, all right?

310
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:02,417
We'll just lose speed if we start
sliding around the road again!

311
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:03,330
I don't care!

312
00:20:03,413 --> 00:20:04,494
Just do it, all right?

313
00:20:04,660 --> 00:20:07,020
I told you, you're wasting your time!

314
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:10,200
Numbers two and three, get
over here on the double!

315
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,760
Hope you like asphalt.

316
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:23,164
Because you're about to get intimately
acquainted with the taste of it real quick.

317
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:28,570
Yahoo!

318
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:31,120
We lost Freaky the Snowman.

319
00:20:31,320 --> 00:20:32,849
Now let's get out of here.

320
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,471
The station's just ahead.

321
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:40,777
We'll grab the disk as planned and
hide before he catches up to us.

322
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:42,340
We can do this, Giorno.

323
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:46,680
A nice plan, but keep dreaming.

324
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:49,037
He'll never make it to the station.

325
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:50,740
Not if I have my way.

326
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:53,477
It's freezing moisture
from the exhaust pipe.

327
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:57,207
Just how cold does it have to
be for that shit to freeze over?

328
00:20:57,400 --> 00:21:00,280
Bastard, here's another dose of hot light.

329
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:04,740
He just popped open the trunk,
which means he's gonna...

330
00:21:06,660 --> 00:21:07,620
This is bad!

331
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:09,331
We've got unwanted cargo!

332
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:10,675
Stop the car, Giorno!

333
00:21:10,780 --> 00:21:13,577
That maniac is gonna try
freezing the brakes again!

334
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:17,600
You should stop wasting your
breath, you gun-bondling kagakatsu!

335
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:23,480
Seeing as how Trish is absent, I
can now do what I came here to do.

336
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:25,950
Shatter!

337
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:35,736
Giorno, your stairs!

338
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:38,980
It only cracked?

339
00:21:39,620 --> 00:21:41,717
What's it going to take to kill him?

340
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:43,460
How do I dissolve his armor?

341
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:46,497
Giorno, could you stand
away from this guy?

342
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:48,080
I can't! Not just yet!

343
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:56,480
We've made it to Venice!

344
00:21:56,760 --> 00:21:58,460
Hang on, we're going in now!

345
00:22:09,860 --> 00:22:16,080
Every time I close my eyes,
I wake up feeling so horny.

346
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:23,397
I can't get you out of my mind,
since you'll be all I see.

347
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:26,437
I would give anything.

348
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:30,537
Just to make you understand me.

349
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:34,837
I don't give a damn about nothing else.

350
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:38,457
Freaking you is all I need.

351
00:22:38,540 --> 00:22:53,377
I need your body.

352
00:22:53,460 --> 00:22:55,500
You won't decide.

353
00:22:57,560 --> 00:22:59,557
You won't decide.

354
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:02,817
You got my mind.

355
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:04,517
You got my mind.

356
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:07,117
I wanna do it for you.

357
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:09,377
What must I say?

358
00:23:09,460 --> 00:23:12,860
What must I do?

359
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:16,860
To show how much.

360
00:23:17,460 --> 00:23:20,457
I'm gonna feed you.

361
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,280
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

362
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:23,540
Just myself.

363
00:23:25,100 --> 00:23:25,930
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

364
00:23:26,013 --> 00:23:27,260
But you must not get it.

365
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,940
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

366
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:56,160
Thank you.
